This is normal because the render function executes every time the component renders:

- Executes once and start fetching the async component
- Once async component is fetched, it renders again
- A **new factory** function is created and start fetching it
- _recursion_

Having the function declared outside is necessary. It's similar to async component being hold in variables vs being passed directly:

```js
const Async = () => import('@/components/Async.vue)

// ...

render (h) {
  // good!
  return h(Async)
}
```

```js
render (h) {
  // does not work because every render creates a new async component
  return h(() => import('Async'))
}
```

```javascript
export default {
  props: ['state'],
  data () {
    return {
      title: this.state
    }
  }
}
```

you assign the prop's value to `title`. this only happens *once*, during mount. If `state` changes later, its changes will not be reflected in `title`.

Solution: use a `computed` instead.

Not a bug. For more help, please visit the communities at forum.vuejs.org // chat.vuejs.org

