https://github.com/zloirock/core-js/blob/v3.9.1/packages/core-js/modules/es.number.constructor.js#L55
Where "NumberWrapper" is the new constructor causing the problem here.

@posva I investigated a little more and came to the conclusion, that this is actually only a problem if there is more than one script on a page including the replacement, since in that case the second script will not find the native constructor anymore and work with a "wrong" native constructor and prototype. If the replacement is globally included only once, this works as expected.

So, you are right, in the end this is indeed a corejs problem, not detecting their own polyfills properly on a second run. :|

So closing this was indeed the right call.

